<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Business</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Business</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-bus</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-bus" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1431?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-bus" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany: Is Saxony-Anhalt's economy really struggling?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64e23ca6cda00144578c9c21a47b5c8a35e0cbd118e68364b744a6eaaef4bd69</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-saxony-anhalt-s-economy-really-struggling/a-78867143--428f69e30327.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-saxony-anhalt-s-economy-really-struggling/a-78867143?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD party has long claimed that the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt has been left behind. Is that really the case? A closer look at the data offers some interesting insights.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>How Volkswagen's huge workforce became a costly burden</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:665f2bd5a40f13cfe05401d29a1fe16950010113523c6dfea662b1e5d1786868</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-volkswagen-s-huge-workforce-became-a-costly-burden/a-77766154--a8906dcb43a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-volkswagen-s-huge-workforce-became-a-costly-burden/a-77766154?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The struggling German carmaker plans to cut up to 100,000 jobs from its 630,000-strong workforce. How did VW's headcount get so bloated, and will the cuts be enough to survive the Chinese EV onslaught?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Is Germany's economic slump finally over?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3518d4c7c92cf73fe3abe12547166f4ab59974b415fb6a08792f95c1384ec744</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T12:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-economic-slump-finally-over/a-78815447--dc14c02fb83d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-economic-slump-finally-over/a-78815447?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite a slew of negative headlines, the German economy has posted its best figures in years. There are reasons for optimism, but structural issues remain.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Can new Apple CEO John Ternus fix the tech giant's AI woes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c288d0026418f6836c9d229c137c4ec6f62a8fcca6f5a094d0b6a685da640887</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898--2304e4feb88d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">John Ternus is just the third Apple CEO in 30 years. His primary challenge is to correct the company's faltering AI strategy to preserve its position as a big tech leader.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Canada's Carney holds firm against Trump tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54f789a2dc785f3d7731c59bf8015fdda2aabbc3da26a00fd6e2400b9d9d2084</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-s-carney-holds-firm-against-trump-tariffs/a-78542754--89c35ddc9034.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-s-carney-holds-firm-against-trump-tariffs/a-78542754?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canada is facing new US import penalties after Prime Minister Mark Carney refused to match US tariffs on China. Other countries are watching as the Trump trade clash turns into a fight over economic sovereignty.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>The great lake divide: Collapse vs. comeback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3dd24ca346144c17c41a8b82c4e9d30326dd5ac77f29191d2ff01faccc7445d</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T09:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-great-lake-divide-collapse-vs-comeback/a-78460263--b2ea5aa30623.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-great-lake-divide-collapse-vs-comeback/a-78460263?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As some of the world's biggest lakes vanish in real time, others are proving that recovery is still within reach.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Why social media addiction is so hard to regulate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee14284bc335357f6c017a0eafe29b3a2aa8026c31ce1676a5d23d47fe079fad</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T09:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-social-media-addiction-is-so-hard-to-regulate/a-78482023--03ceaea9fb93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-social-media-addiction-is-so-hard-to-regulate/a-78482023?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facebook, Instagram and other social media platforms are accused of deliberately fostering addictive behavior among young users. Yet regulators continue to struggle to rein in their engagement-driven business models.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Gamescom 2026: What's next for the gaming industry?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38588314b58206b57a7bce4b0ca58d3fa903b59874f56614535c5da15f327cd1</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T11:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gamescom-2026-what-s-next-for-the-gaming-industry/a-78502849--158dcd55c502.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gamescom-2026-what-s-next-for-the-gaming-industry/a-78502849?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Gamescom 2026 opens in Cologne, AI, hardware costs and slowing user growth are putting pressure on the global games industry despite its current strength.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why Germany's Volkswagen could cut 100,000 jobs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:802335423514a86697724979d14772d2d5016bbc37b4d87167c49bdf5b5fb0cb</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T13:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-volkswagen-could-cut-100-000-jobs/a-78483715--9335697d1887.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-volkswagen-could-cut-100-000-jobs/a-78483715?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Europe's biggest automaker, Volkswagen, faces Chinese competition, high costs and US tariffs. What could its restructuring mean for the German car industry?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Can new US sanctions cripple Iran's shadow economy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab5fe5907385770ae7a1f59b198dd16b34b822773bf105cbceb63e19c07832e0</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-new-us-sanctions-cripple-iran-s-shadow-economy/a-78494630--0605fdb5b60c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-new-us-sanctions-cripple-iran-s-shadow-economy/a-78494630?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is expanding sanctions on Iran's financial networks, targeting crypto, gold, aviation and shipping. DW spoke with analysts about what could change.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Spiraling health costs force Iranians to delay care</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec3f0d565b37ae97650d6e24651a6645025eb3c9cc1900c798974e63391a2288</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spiraling-health-costs-force-iranians-to-delay-care/a-78455430--9b49d45ffc01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spiraling-health-costs-force-iranians-to-delay-care/a-78455430?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A single chemotherapy session in Iran can cost six times the monthly minimum wage. As drug prices soar and medicine is in short supply, doctors say more patients are delaying or abandoning treatment.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why Germany's gas storage levels are so low</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0fe794060428d8d835ce798cd23e6cec5d3f94e2da639bd39a733834bb5d7fa3</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T14:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-gas-storage-levels-are-so-low/a-78440677--0cf8a2f6bb58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-gas-storage-levels-are-so-low/a-78440677?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's gas storage facilities are only 50% full as traders bet that wholesale prices will fall if the Iran war ends. With around three months until winter, DW asks whether the country can refill its reserves in time.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Evergrande founder Hui Ka Yan sentenced to life in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3244d1f2672e5275178ea00452f7d09c94962a29e0350b4a4569f21f91a3d29</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T07:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/evergrande-founder-hui-ka-yan-sentenced-to-life-in-prison/a-78439153--1b7d4bee30d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/evergrande-founder-hui-ka-yan-sentenced-to-life-in-prison/a-78439153?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Chinese court ordered the former billionaire's assets to be confiscated and fined Evergrande-related companies billions of dollars.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Who really owns the Caspian Sea?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5ba7c9b9835d5934649e031f7a88494cd1fbf8b496d8e914a5caad906eaaeba</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T09:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-really-owns-the-caspian-sea/a-78396946--9894c6169af9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-really-owns-the-caspian-sea/a-78396946?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Five countries border the Caspian Sea, but none owns a fixed share. A 2018 convention established rules for navigation, security and fishing while leaving some seabed borders unresolved.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Will Germany's drought push up food prices?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ec98af508f3625275969eaaacc565ecfad4764c87fa4cc8bcc3d38b83bb65b7</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T14:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-germany-s-drought-push-up-food-prices/a-78408203--34270750f888.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-germany-s-drought-push-up-food-prices/a-78408203?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's main farmers' association has warned of a below-average harvest after drought and crops damaged by extreme heat. DW looks into what lower yields could mean for food prices and grocery bills.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Norway wealth fund sounds alarm on AI stock market bubble</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25e0d6985b9b5edab1f6255813d9070cd6ced09855e9c4dc027a1d1cfecb8280</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-17T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-wealth-fund-sounds-alarm-on-ai-stock-market-bubble/a-78351371--3c0b465876b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-wealth-fund-sounds-alarm-on-ai-stock-market-bubble/a-78351371?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The head of Norway's sovereign wealth fund has warned that soaring AI-driven stock valuations could trigger a sharp correction. How exposed is the world's largest sovereign wealth fund to a market downturn?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>EU waste packaging rules: Why small businesses are worried</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab88be23043e2f338861d9484334bd884e6c5373d3f46a28d117c965e5a940d5</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-12T09:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-waste-packaging-rules-why-small-businesses-are-worried/a-78326555--1999ee3867ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-waste-packaging-rules-why-small-businesses-are-worried/a-78326555?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU has introduced new rules targeting packaging waste and "forever chemicals." Although the changes will be phased in slowly, some small sellers have already paused shipments due to the additional red tape.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>How the Rhine drought threatens Germany's economic recovery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0acdf2acfa2ea6af7be275734769bda5387d26aabd0155a474a53df2ee09f27</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-10T15:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-the-rhine-drought-threatens-germany-s-economic-recovery/a-78300076--a571816e5435.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-the-rhine-drought-threatens-germany-s-economic-recovery/a-78300076?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's inland waterways still move around 5% of the nation's goods. With the Rhine at a critically low level, DW explores how the drought is hitting the economy where it hurts most.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why is Russia selling its gold?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84bd46bbc79307103b93c4f456c87c9e35d527d36dd18fb885c988ff444f26fb</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-06T08:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-is-russia-selling-its-gold/a-78145069--3a10f821619a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-is-russia-selling-its-gold/a-78145069?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia has become one of the world's biggest sellers of gold over the past 12 months. It's an attempt to raise cash in the face of budget issues, but not necessarily a sign of a looming financial crisis.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>AI ecosystem's 'circular' investment: risk or advantage?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ada4180c2c37e8ea5735a6917c295f0140493c426647bda9ed76330931f37ac</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-05T06:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-ecosystem-s-circular-investment-risk-or-advantage/a-78186917--a87bdbfbe6f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-ecosystem-s-circular-investment-risk-or-advantage/a-78186917?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amid talk of an AI sector bubble, one aspect is under scrutiny. Many big AI players are invested in smaller ones, who then buy the bigger firm's products. This brings risks and advantages.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry></feed>
